# Member Notification Inbox — Platform Charter (MNI-001)

**Purpose:** Define the **shared, domain-agnostic** durable in-app notification inbox for all member-facing surfaces. Ticketing, booking/tour, payment/debt, and wallet **must** write to this boundary — not to module-specific inbox tables as the final contract.

---

## 1. Architecture unlock (explicit authorization)

| Field                         | Value                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Unlock ID**                 | `IMPL-SK2.D+`                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| **Authorized by**             | Product owner / Architect (user chat authorization)                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Date**                      | 2026-09-04                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| **Scope**                     | `ticketing-system-complete` full closure on branch `feature/ticketing-system`                                                                                                                                       |
| **Decision**                  | Implement unified Postgres `member_notifications` + `member_notification_deliveries`; migrate ticketing and DP-4 booking/finance writers; expose `/member/notifications` aggregate API and portal cross-domain bell |
| **Supersedes for new writes** | `ticket_notifications` as final inbox design (historical rows retained; new writes target `member_notifications`)                                                                                                   |
| **SK2 reconciliation**        | See [SK2_D_MEMBER_INBOX.md](../phase-saas-kernel/appendices/SK2_D_MEMBER_INBOX.md)                                                                                                                                  |

**This unlock is recorded in this document.** No prior `IMPL-SK2.D+` existed before this authorization.

---

## 2. Non-goals

- Marketing campaign / bulk email product
- Operator session authority (PCMS-001 unchanged)
- Replacing outbox as transport SoT (SK2)
- Hollow `packages/notification-kernel` package

---

## 3. Data model

### 3.1 `member_notifications`

| Column          | Type         | Rule                                                      |
| --------------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `id`            | UUID         | PK                                                        |
| `tenant_id`     | UUID         | RLS scope; from auth context                              |
| `user_id`       | UUID         | Recipient member                                          |
| `source_module` | text         | `ticketing` \| `booking` \| `finance` \| `wallet`         |
| `event_type`    | text         | Domain outbox event type                                  |
| `entity_type`   | text         | `ticket` \| `registration` \| `payment` \| `wallet_event` |
| `entity_id`     | UUID?        | Primary entity reference (nullable when N/A)              |
| `title`         | text         | Rendered or fallback title                                |
| `body`          | text         | Rendered or fallback body                                 |
| `title_key`     | text?        | i18n key when template-driven                             |
| `body_key`      | text?        | i18n key when template-driven                             |
| `template_key`  | text?        | Opaque template id                                        |
| `dedupe_key`    | text         | Stable idempotency key (typically `domainEventId`)        |
| `payload`       | jsonb        | Event context for UI deep links                           |
| `read_at`       | timestamptz? | Member read timestamp                                     |
| `created_at`    | timestamptz  | Insert time                                               |

**Unique:** `(tenant_id, user_id, dedupe_key)` — idempotent inbox insert per recipient.

**RLS:** `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`; policy `tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id')::uuid`.

### 3.2 `member_notification_deliveries`

Async email/SMS channel retries keyed to `member_notifications`. Same retry semantics as legacy `ticket_notification_deliveries`.

---

## 4. HTTP API

| Method | Path                                  | Scope                                        |
| ------ | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/member/notifications`               | Member aggregate inbox (all `source_module`) |
| GET    | `/member/notifications/unread-count`  | Cross-domain unread badge                    |
| PATCH  | `/member/notifications/:id/read`      | Mark one read                                |
| POST   | `/member/notifications/mark-all-read` | Mark all read for recipient                  |

**Legacy aliases** (ticketing-filtered, deprecated): `/member/ticket-notifications/*` delegate to repository with `sourceModule=ticketing` filter until portal migration completes.

---

## 5. Writers (outbox dispatchers)

| Module       | Dispatcher                                                                                                                                                      | `source_module` | `entity_type`  |
| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | -------------- |
| Ticketing    | `dispatch-ticket-notification-from-outbox.ts`                                                                                                                   | `ticketing`     | `ticket`       |
| Booking/tour | `dispatch-member-notification-from-outbox.ts`                                                                                                                   | `booking`       | `registration` |
| Payment/debt | same dispatcher (finance events)                                                                                                                                | `finance`       | `payment`      |
| Wallet       | `dispatch-wallet-notification-from-outbox.ts` + `PrismaWalletRepository.persistMutation` outbox enqueue (`wallet.transaction.posted`, `wallet.refund.credited`) | `wallet`        | `wallet_event` |

All dispatchers call `insertMemberNotificationRow` in `member-notification.repository.ts`.

---

## 6. Portal integration

- Bell badge: `GET /member/notifications/unread-count` (cross-domain)
- List page: `/me/notifications` → BFF `/api/me/notifications`
- Deep links: `payload` + `entity_type` + `entity_id` drive navigation (ticket → `/me/tickets/:id`, etc.)

---

## 7. Testing requirements

| Suite                                   | Proves                                                                                                                                                                 |
| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `member-notifications.postgres.spec.ts` | RLS, dedupe, cross-module list; **relay** proofs for booking (`registration.approved`), finance (`payment.hold.scheduled`), wallet (`operatorCredit` → outbox → inbox) |
| `ticket-notifications.postgres.spec.ts` | Ticketing path regression + relay dedupe via shared table                                                                                                              |
| Portal E2E                              | Bell + list after operator reply                                                                                                                                       |
| Axe specs                               | No serious/critical violations (scoped ticketing regions; executed 2026-09-04 adversarial pass)                                                                        |

---

## 8. Migration from `ticket_notifications`

1. New writes → `member_notifications` only.
2. Historical `ticket_notifications` rows remain readable via legacy routes during transition.
3. No destructive drop of `ticket_notifications` in this tranche.

---

_MNI-001 — platform charter filed with explicit IMPL-SK2.D+ user authorization 2026-09-04._
